            <ArticleTitle>Norovirus GII.17 Natural Infections in Rhesus Monkeys, China.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>316-319</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid2302.161077</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Noroviruses are a leading viral cause of acute gastroenteritis among humans. During the 2014-15 epidemic season, norovirus GII.17 was detected in rhesus monkeys in China. Genetic, structural, and challenge studies revealed virus mutations and verified the infections. Thus, cross-species transmission may occur, and monkeys may be a virus reservoir.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
